-- title:
--   Ramification of a complex place dictionary equals half the ±Γ-stabiliser order
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be a finite-index subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ containing $T=\begin{pmatrix}1&1\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, and let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}\subseteq\mathbb{Q}((q))$ assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101), the subfield generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by all quotients of the integral $q$-expansion series of two modular forms of one weight on $\Gamma$ (with nonzero denominator). Let $D$ be a `ComplexPlaceDictionaryOf Γ F₀`, that is: a map $\mathrm{pt}$ from the upper half-plane $\mathcal{H}$ to places of the intermediate field $\mathbb{C}F_0\subseteq\mathbb{C}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of $F_0$ (a valuation subring containing $\mathbb{C}$, proper, and a principal ideal ring), a positive integer-valued function $\tau\mapsto e_\tau$, invariance $\mathrm{pt}(\gamma\cdot\tau)=\mathrm{pt}(\tau)$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma$, the description of the valuation subring of $\mathrm{pt}(\tau)$ as those $x$ whose level-$\Gamma$ realization $\mathrm{realizeOf}$ is bounded near $\tau$ on punctured neighbourhoods, and, for $x\neq 0$, the identity $\operatorname{ord}_\tau$ of that realization $=e_\tau\cdot\operatorname{ord}_{\mathrm{pt}(\tau)}(x)$ as meromorphic order at $\tau$. Assume further that $\mathrm{pt}$ separates $\Gamma$-orbits: $\mathrm{pt}(\tau)=\mathrm{pt}(\tau')$ implies $\tau'=\gamma\cdot\tau$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma$. Then for every $\tau\in\mathcal{H}$, $2e_\tau$ equals the cardinality of the stabiliser of $\tau$ in the subgroup $\Gamma\vee\langle -1\rangle$ of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$.
--
--   This identifies the ramification datum of a complex place dictionary with the ramification index at $\tau$ of the quotient map $\mathcal{H}\to X(\Gamma)$, namely the order of the image in $\mathrm{PSL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the stabiliser of $\tau$ in $\pm\Gamma$; it is thus the bridge between orders of vanishing of modular forms on $\mathcal{H}$ and valuations at the corresponding places of the function field. It is used for the computation of divisors of Hecke-type functions at a single point and, specialised to $\Gamma=\Gamma_H(M)$, gives the corresponding statement for that level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_ComplexPlaceDictionaryOf_two_mul_ramification_eq_card_stabilizer.lean

